              <div class="report-heading">ULTRASONOGRAPHY ABD AND PEL FEMALENK</div>
              <div class="report-body-text">SONOGRAPHY –  ABDOMEN & PELVIS
 
LIVER :-  Liver appears normal in size, shape & echogenicity. No focal lesions are noted.  Intrahepatic portal & biliary radicals appear normal. Portal vein is normal (<PV> mm).

GALL BLADDER :-  Gall Bladder is distended & appears normal.  No calculus or mass lesion is noted.  Wall thickness appears normal.
CBD is normal in course & calibre (<CBD> mm).

SPLEEN :-  Spleen appears normal in size (<SPLEEN> cm), shape & echotexture. No focal lesions are noted.  Splenic vein appears normal.

PANCREAS :- Pancreas appears normal in size, shape & echogenicity.

KIDNEYS:-   Both kidneys appear normal in size & shape. No mass lesion is noted.  Parenchymal echogenicity & corticomedullary ratio is normal. Parenchymal thickness appears normal.                                           
Right kidney measures  <RT_K>  cm. Left kidney measures <LT_K> cm.
No calculus or hydronephrosis is noted.

URINARY BLADDER :- Urinary Bladder is distended.  No mass lesion or calculus is noted.  Bladder wall thickness appears normal. 
Prevoid vol ~ <PREVOID> cc, Post void vol ~ <POSTVOID> cc. No significant post void residue.

UTERUS: - Uterus is <VERTED>verted, normal in size, shape & echotexture. It measures <UTERUS> cm. No fibroids are noted. Endometrial canal is in midline & measures <ET> mm.

OVARIES: - Both ovaries are normal in size & shape
Right ovary measures <RO> cm , Left ovary measures <LO> cm.
	No obvious  lymphadenopathy / ascites noted.
	No mass lesion or collection is noted in both iliac fossa. 
	Visualised large bowel loops are filled with excessive gases.

</div>

